---
/** /review-policy/: independence, review units, updates and corrections. */
import { site } from '~/config/site';
import { minTestDays } from '~/config/editorial';
import TrustLayout from '~/layouts/TrustLayout.astro';

const toc = [
  { id: 'independence', label: 'Independence' },
  { id: 'review-units', label: 'Review units' },
  { id: 'updates', label: 'Updates' },
  { id: 'corrections', label: 'Corrections' },
];
---

<TrustLayout
  title="Review policy"
  description={`How ${site.name} keeps reviews independent: review units, sponsorship, updates and corrections.`}
  path="/review-policy/"
  updated={site.legal.updated}
  toc={toc}
>
  <div class="prose max-w-[72ch]">
    <h2 id="independence">Independence</h2>
    <p>
      Our writers decide what to review and what score to give. Brands, retailers and advertisers
      never see a review before it is published, cannot buy a rating or a place in a buying guide,
      and cannot ask us to change or remove one.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not publish sponsored reviews. If we ever publish content paid for by a brand, it will
      be labelled "Sponsored" at the top and will not carry a rating.
    </p>

    <h2 id="review-units">Review units</h2>
    <p>
      Some products are lent to us by the brand; others we buy ourselves. Loaned units are returned
      when testing ends. Either way we test them the same way, for at least {minTestDays} days,
      following our <a href="/how-we-test/">test plans</a>. We do not accept gifts in exchange for
      coverage.
    </p>

    <h2 id="updates">Updates</h2>
    <p>
      Prices and availability in India change often. We re-check buying guides every month and
      update reviews when a software update, a price change or a new rival changes our advice. The
      date at the top of an article shows when it was last updated.
    </p>

    <h2 id="corrections">Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      If we get something wrong, we fix it and add a note at the bottom of the article saying what
      changed and when. If you spot a mistake, please <a href="/contact/">tell us</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</TrustLayout>
